 erties of high-dimensional electroencephalogram (HD-EEG) signals contain v
 aluable information about brain activity and functioning. These properties
  tend to vary over time and are characterized through the time-varying spe
 ctral density. Rather than analyzing the time-varying spectral density dir
 ectly\, biomedical researchers work with low-dime\nCategory: Academic\nOri
 ginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/statistics-seminar-series-ad
 aptive-frequency-band-learning-of-nonstationary-functional-time-series-an-
 application-to-high-dimensional-eeg-signals
