SUMMARY:Astrobiology and the Law: What Policies are Needed to Protect Extr
 aterrestrial Life? — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261120T140000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261120T153000
DTSTAMP:20261114T063117Z
UID:bc89ee8dd02d5f39100b29b6b549@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Lectures & Speakers\,Washington\, DC\,United St
 ates
DESCRIPTION:Astrobiology and the Law: What Policies are Needed to Protect 
 Extraterrestrial Life? The question of whether there is life on other plan
 ets is one of the most profound and enduring mysteries. The study of life 
 in the universe is the purview of the discipline known as astrobiology.  
 Since the Viking Mission in the 1970s we have been searching for life on o
 ther planets like Mars or moons like Enceladus and Europa in our solar sys
 tem. And we are preparing to continue those searches with both manned and 
 unmanned missions in the near future. But are we psychologically\, sociolo
 gically\, and morally prepared to find extraterrestrial life – even micr
 obes – and behave in a way that will not violate th\nCategory: Lectures 
 & Speakers\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/astrobiology-
 and-the-law-what-policies-are-needed-to-protect-extraterrestrial-life
LOCATION:George Washington University\, Washington\, DC
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/astrobiology-and-the-law-what-policies-
 are-needed-to-protect-extraterrestrial-life
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
