DESCRIPTION:What Do We Mean By PrEP? Featuring Dr. Maranda Ward\, '17 \, A
 ssociate Professor and Director of Equity\, Department of Clinical Researc
 h & Leadership\, GW School of Medicine and Health Sciences PrEP\, or Pre-E
 xposure Prophylaxis\, is a safe and highly effective medication that helps
  prevent HIV infection. Yet many people and communities who could benefit 
 from PrEP are not using it. Why? In this talk\, Dr. Maranda Ward will expl
 ore how public health messaging\, research\, and healthcare practices shap
 e people's understanding of PrEP and influence who feels seen\, supported
 \, and informed when making decisions about HIV prevention. Drawing on her
  research\, Dr. Ward will discuss the importance of moving \nCategory: Lec
