BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cracks & Reforms: The 1920s Through the GW Collection — Washingt
 on\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261202T130000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261202T170000
DTSTAMP:20261114T063117Z
UID:f2fe4e37c39da219a1d2c77f825f@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:The 1920s emerged as a decade suspended between collapse and r
 econstruction\, an era marked by “cracks and reforms” that ushered in 
 a profound reconfiguration of the visual world.  During this period marke
 d by civil transformation and political upheaval\, artists\, journalists\,
  and makers had opportunities to reconstruct both individual and collectiv
 e identities. A century later\, Cracks & Reforms presents a distinct cross
 -section of this period\, revealing global currents of migration\, moderni
 zation\, and cultural redefinition through the lens of the GW Collection. 
 Students led by Associate Professor Bibiana Obler selected works to study 
 and exhibit\, their research eventually leading to unified t\nCategory: Ar
 ts & Culture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/cracks-refo
 rms-the-1920s-through-the-gw-collection
LOCATION:Flagg Building\, 500 17th Street NW\, Washington DC 20006
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/cracks-reforms-the-1920s-through-the-gw
 -collection
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eric Gottesman’s NIGHT AND DAY — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261202T130000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261202T170000
DTSTAMP:20261114T063117Z
UID:1dbb76a929ae768f571ad69564c9@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:For Freedoms presents artist and educator Eric Gottesman’s N
 IGHT AND DAY which centers on Ethiopian journalist and author Baalu Girma
 ’s controversial 1984 Amharic novel Oromay \, written under the Derg reg
 ime and banned shortly after its publication. Drawing on Gottesman’s dee
 p engagement with the novel\, NIGHT AND DAY considers how artists create\,
  communicate\, and sustain cultural memory within and against conditions o
 f censorship\, political repression\, and state violence. The exhibition e
 xtends beyond the gallery through a library of banned books\, a self-guide
 d workshop station that invites visitors to respond to censorship through 
 writing and drawing\, and a public conversation on how artist\nCategory: A
 rts & Culture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/eric-gotte
 smans-night-and-day
LOCATION:Flagg Building\, 500 17th Street NW\, Washington DC 20006
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/eric-gottesmans-night-and-day
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
