SUMMARY:Food\, Flow\, Photography Gallery Presentation — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261204T130000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261204T150000
DTSTAMP:20261114T063117Z
UID:bcd0b48dfb63603938e43854f3ac@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Exhibition\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:All are invited to a photographic poster presentation where st
 udents in the Food\, Flow\, Photography course will showcase their final p
 rojects! This unique class\, supported by the Global Food Institute \, Mec
 hanical & Aerospace Engineering \, and Corcoran School of the Arts & Desig
 n \, brings science and art together. Students reveal the hidden physics o
 f fluid flows (gases and liquids) through the art of cooking. They experim
 ented with techniques to visualize flows in soups\, sauces\, mocktails\, c
 offee\, tea\, caramelization\, and more. It is science you can see and art
  you can feel. Mark your calendar and prepare to be amazed!\nCategory: Exh
 ibition\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/food-flow-photog
 raphy-gallery26
LOCATION:Science & Engineering Hall\, 800 22nd Street NW\, Washington DC 2
 0052
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/food-flow-photography-gallery26
